<%# ONE COPYABLE WORKFLOW PHRASE — a soul's heartbeat ("Carl Heartbeat") or one of its
    acts ("pr-review"). Shared by the soul launcher (tasks/_heartbeat_launcher, the
    Workflows sidebar) and the Workflows summary card's carousel, so a chip copies,
    flashes and wraps the same way wherever it is drawn.

    Its OWN button, its OWN data-clip and its OWN Alpine `copied` flash. The phrase is
    server-rendered into data-clip AND the visible <code> so tests and the
    no-clipboard fallback read it. Being a real <button>, it also owns its click inside
    a summary card: deploySummary().openFrom ignores clicks that start on one.

    Locals:
      text      the phrase to copy
      row_kind  "heartbeat" (row 1) or "action"
      extra_class  optional classes for the button (width, etc.) %>
<% text = local_assigns.fetch(:text) %>
<% row_kind = local_assigns.fetch(:row_kind) %>
<% leading = row_kind == "heartbeat" ? "❤️" : action_icon(text) %>
<button type="button"
        x-data="{ copied: false }"
        class="group relative flex w-full min-w-0 items-center justify-start gap-1.5 rounded-md border border-subtle bg-inset px-1.5 py-1 transition hover:border-primary/40 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-primary/50 <%= local_assigns[:extra_class] %>"
        :class="copied ? 'border-mint-400/60' : ''"
        data-clip="<%= text %>"
        data-row="<%= row_kind %>"
        @click="window.copyText($el.dataset.clip); copied = true; setTimeout(() => copied = false, 1400)"
        :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied!' : '<%= j "Copy: #{text}" %>'"
        title="<%= "Copy: #{text}" %>">
  <%# Leading icon: heart for the soul heartbeat (row 1); each action gets its
      own glyph — a keycap 1-3 for the ordered release actions, a themed emoji
      for the rest. Decorative — NOT part of the copied data-clip text. %>
  <% if leading %>
    <span class="shrink-0 text-[10px] leading-none" aria-hidden="true"
          data-test="<%= row_kind == "heartbeat" ? "heartbeat-heart" : "action-icon" %>"><%= leading %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%# The two row kinds wrap DIFFERENTLY, and the difference is the whole point.
      An ACT is a single hyphenated token — `production-deploy` — and CSS treats a
      hyphen as a break opportunity, so ordinary wrapping splits it into
      "production-" / "deploy", which reads as two commands. Acts therefore get
      `truncate` (nowrap + ellipsis); every act registered today fits on one line
      wherever a chip is drawn, so the ellipsis is a safety net for a longer future
      act, never the normal case.
      ROW 1 is a PHRASE — "Turf Monster Heartbeat" — and in a narrow column it cannot
      fit on one line at a readable size. So it is allowed to wrap, but only at its
      SPACES: `break-words` is deliberately absent, so a word is never split mid-token.
      Two tidy lines beat an unreadable one.
      Either way nothing is lost — the full phrase is in data-clip (what actually
      gets copied), in the title tooltip, and in the DOM text the tests read. %>
  <code class="min-w-0 text-left text-[9px] font-normal normal-case leading-tight tracking-normal text-body <%= "truncate" if row_kind == "action" %>"><%= text %></code>
  <span class="pointer-events-none absolute right-1 top-1 text-[9px] text-mint-300"
        x-show="copied" x-cloak x-transition.opacity>&check;</span>
</button>
